& [ExportedRuntimeBoundaryContract] is the runtime authority boundary exported by FSC3
  + [graph_state_role] is execution_state_only
  + [checkpoint_state_role] is execution_state_only
  + [source_authority_role] is SOP files and accepted packs remain source of truth
  + [forbidden_mutation] is accepted pack edit, canonical authority edit, checkpoint authority promotion, hidden graph write, surface authority promotion, or operations control
  + [stale_trigger] is changed FSC2 pack, changed FSC3 slice surface, changed runtime invariant, changed graph contract, changed interrupt contract, changed trace proof, changed imported operator contract, false-ready checkpoint, hidden graph write, or missing operator_trace

  = must: force downstream surface projection to display authority_notice when runtime output is derived or staleable

& [ExportedWholeFieldPlannerGraphContract] is the graph contract exported by FSC3
  + [graph_contract] is WholeFieldPlannerGraphContractV1
  + [state_contract] is GraphStateContract
  + [node_contract_set] is GraphNodeContractSet
  + [edge_contract_set] is GraphEdgeContractSet
  + [checkpoint_policy] is CheckpointPolicy
  + [authority_policy] is RuntimeAuthorityReadWritePolicy
  + [refusal_contract] is RuntimeRefusalContract
  + [terminal_outcome] is terminal_success
  + [terminal_outcome] is terminal_blocked
  + [terminal_outcome] is terminal_stale
  + [terminal_outcome] is terminal_fault
  + [terminal_outcome] is terminal_interrupt

  = must: keep blocked, stale, fault, and interrupt paths terminal until accepted retry or resume evidence exists
  = must: make every future runtime implementation prove conformance before surface consumption

& [ExportedSOPFirstInterruptContract] is the interrupt and resume contract exported by FSC3
  + [interrupt_contract] is SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1
  + [interrupt_kind] is ambiguous_identity
  + [interrupt_kind] is authority_conflict
  + [interrupt_kind] is stale_input
  + [interrupt_kind] is missing_proof_route
  + [interrupt_kind] is contested_coordination_claim
  + [interrupt_kind] is unsupported_scope
  + [interrupt_kind] is high_risk_operation
  + [interrupt_kind] is human_override_required
  + [interrupt_kind] is checkpoint_authority_confusion
  + [required_context] is InterruptContextPacket
  + [resume_condition_contract] is ResumeConditionContract
  + [no_hidden_mutation_rule] is NoHiddenMutationRule

  = must: prevent future projections from rendering an interrupted runtime path as completed work
  = must: preserve enough context for another conversation, model, or human to decide the resume route

